Adam Stegerwald has been elected as the chairman of the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party's**</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?]. He seems to represent a rightward turn from Marx, despite his trade union background, and will preside over a [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party's**</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?] less inclined to compromise with the left. He views the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party's**</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?] as a prototype for a <span style="color: #000000;">Christian</span>, <span style="color: #586593;">democratic</span>, <span style="color: #000000;">German</span>, and <span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> party, and aims to transform it according to the principles laid out in his proposed "Essen program" eight years prior. 

